# There is no build step and no dependency here, so almost nothing needs
# ignoring: everything in this repository is either the page, the data it
# reads, or something CI runs. Nothing generated is listed below because
# nothing is generated, and nothing the published page serves is listed
# either - wai_data.csv, wai_meta.json and vendor/ are all fetched by
# index.html at run time and must stay tracked.

# macOS Finder metadata and resource forks
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows Explorer thumbnail and folder-view caches
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Linux file-manager folder settings
.directory

# Per-developer editor state. Not part of the project, and different for
# whoever opens it.
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
*.swp

# npm installs nothing into this directory. CI's only npm call is
# `npx html-validate index.html`, which resolves into npm's own cache
# elsewhere - html-validate is deliberately never declared as a dependency,
# because CI must not be the thing that introduces one into a repository
# that has none.
#
# These two lines are therefore not an invitation to add a package.json.
# They are there so that a local `npm install`, run once while debugging
# that command, cannot put several thousand files into a commit. A stray
# package.json is left visible on purpose: it is one reviewable line in a
# diff, and it should be noticed rather than silently ignored.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
